# tools/entry_names.allow -- the sites tools/entry_names_check.rb lets name an entry by hand.
# CLASS<TAB>file<TAB>the site's line (stripped, as in the source)<TAB>why no String kind can name a deleted bytes entry here
#   NUM   an Int, Float or numeric kind: the store has no String form
#   POLY  the container holds boxed (Poly) values
#   ARM   a String kind is taken by an earlier arm, or the suffix is the row's (hsfx and kin)
#   READ  the operation is a read or an aggregate (get, oget, to_a, intersect, ...), not a store or a search a String has an `_e` form of

